{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyDerivative","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetVol_strictConcaveOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetVol_strictConcaveOn","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L257-L325","doc":"**The Lobachevsky ideal-tetrahedron volume is strictly concave on the open\nangle simplex.**  This is the analytic content of `qou-krvm` hypothesis (iv) for\nthe single-tetrahedron case: the volume functional is strictly concave, hence has\na unique maximiser, on the angle-structure polytope.  Symmetry-invariance is\n`tetVol_symm₁₂` (and its `S₃` companions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.lineVol_strictConcaveOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lineVol_strictConcaveOn","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L238-L253","doc":"The line restriction is strictly concave on `[0,1]`, provided the whole\nsegment `s ↦ (x₁+s v₁, x₂+s v₂)` for `s ∈ [0,1]` stays in the good set and the\ndirection is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.deriv2_lineVol_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.deriv2_lineVol_neg","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L220-L236","doc":"`deriv (deriv (lineVol …)) s` equals the Hessian quadratic form at direction\n`(v₁, v₂)`, and is `< 0` whenever `(v₁, v₂) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_deriv_lineVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_deriv_lineVol","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L183-L218","doc":"Second derivative of the line restriction on the good set — the\nnegative-definite Hessian quadratic form in the direction `(v₁, v₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_lineVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_lineVol","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L160-L181","doc":"First derivative of the line restriction on the good set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.lineVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lineVol","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L155-L158","doc":"The restriction `g(s) = Λ(A s) + Λ(B s) + Λ(C s)` along the line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.isOpen_lineGood","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.isOpen_lineGood","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L137-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.lineGood","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lineGood","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L129-L135","doc":"The three angle coordinates along the line `s ↦ (x₁ + s v₁, x₂ + s v₂)` all\nlie in `(0, π)` — the good set on which `g = V ∘ line` is twice differentiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.convex_tetSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.convex_tetSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L113-L125","doc":"The simplex is convex (a finite intersection of open half-planes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetVol_symm₁₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetVol_symm₁₂","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L83-L88","doc":"`V` is symmetric under the `α ↔ β` swap.  With the third angle\n`γ = π - α - β` also symmetric, this is one generator of the `S₃` symmetry of the\nvolume; the volume is invariant under every angle permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetSimplex","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L78-L81","doc":"The open angle simplex `{α > 0, β > 0, α + β < π}` — the interior of the\nCasson–Rivin angle-structure polytope for the single ideal tetrahedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetVol","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcave.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The Lobachevsky volume of the ideal tetrahedron with angle coordinates\n`(p.1, p.2)` (third angle `π - p.1 - p.2`): `V(α,β) = Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(π-α-β)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}